Use the cross product of the vector from the first point to the second with the vector from the first point to each later point. If every cross product is zero, all points are collinear. This avoids division, so vertical lines need no special case.

```python
from typing import List

class Solution:
    def checkStraightLine(self, coordinates: List[List[int]]) -> bool:
        x0, y0 = coordinates[0]
        x1, y1 = coordinates[1]
        dx, dy = x1 - x0, y1 - y0
        for x, y in coordinates[2:]:
            if dx * (y - y0) != dy * (x - x0):
                return False
        return True
```

