Put `nums` in a set, then walk the list once. A component starts at a node whose value is in the set when the previous node was not in the set (or there is no previous node). Counting those starts gives the number of components.

```python
class Solution:
    def numComponents(self, head: Optional[ListNode], nums: List[int]) -> int:
        s = set(nums)
        count = 0
        in_comp = False
        node = head
        while node:
            if node.val in s:
                if not in_comp:
                    count += 1
                    in_comp = True
            else:
                in_comp = False
            node = node.next
        return count
```

